<title>GERMANY: Linotype sees 96 loss, to cut 1,200 jobs.</title>
<headline>Linotype sees 96 loss, to cut 1,200 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German printing systems maker Linotype-Hell AG said on Friday it would make a loss of about 70 million marks ($45.4 million) in 1996 and would cut 1,200 jobs in a major restructuring to be completed by end-1997.</p>
<p>The company, whose shares were suspended earlier on Friday pending the announcement, said earnings would be hit hard by the increasingly difficult market situation worldwide in the printing products industry.</p>
<p>($ = 1.541 German Marks)  </p>
<p>Under the revamp Linotype will concentrate on its core business and centralise all activities at its Kiel production site, the company said.</p>
<p>Linotype was taken over by printing machinery group Heidelberger Druckmaschinen AG earlier this year. Heidelberger Druck is in turn a subsidiary of Rheinelektra AG.</p>
<p>&quot;All measures will be completed by the end of the coming year at the latest,&quot; Linotype said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
